# So the typed form asks the cell alone and ONE BYTE OF THAT MEMBER, not the byte of the class, which any write on any prototype above sets for the rest of the process:
# lay() lays a name that has nothing to do with either; replace() replaces both, and the closed arm finds what was laid; put back, the bytes stay set and the built-ins answer through the closed arm.
